#N canvas 20 20 3400 2400 12;
#X text 20 20 m_fm1 -- the M-VAVE FM-1's device layer \, and the only file that talks to it. Output-only: its own keys are left unwired (wire.sh) \, so nothing is decoded and nothing goes on param. ref/device/fm1.md, f 84;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: the Pd channel the FM-1's own channel 1 lands on (49 on the device) \, required. inlet 1: selector-prefixed -- notes <note> <vel> <dur> \, cc <controller> <value> \, program <n> \, note <note> <vel> \, byte <b>. outlets: none., f 84;
#X text 20 250 Wired from u_map \, not sent: no bus carries a sounding note (C-2). Selector-prefixed \, so a new capability costs one route argument here and nothing in u_map or u_root (ref/architecture.md)., f 84;
#X obj 20 460 inlet;
#X obj 20 540 route notes cc program note byte;
#X obj 20 660 unpack f f f;
#X obj 20 800 makenote;
#X obj 20 1000 noteout;
#X obj 460 660 unpack f f;
#X obj 460 740 t b f;
#X obj 460 830 f;
#X obj 460 1000 ctlout;
#X obj 900 660 + 1;
#X obj 900 1000 pgmout;
#X obj 1300 660 t b;
#X msg 1300 730 fail m_fm1 bad-selector;
#X obj 1300 800 s err;
#X obj 1780 900 loadbang;
#X obj 1780 950 f \$1;
#X obj 1780 1000 t f f f f;
#X text 1780 1060 The channel goes in cold \, off the right outlets \, before any value can arrive \, and not as a creation argument: Pd 0.49 does not warn about an extra one (item 63)., f 60;
#X text 20 1080 unpack fires right to left \, so duration and velocity are in makenote before the note triggers it. makenote owns the note-offs \, so a dropped cord or a reload cannot leave the FM-1 droning., f 60;
#X text 460 1100 The t b f is load-bearing: ctlout's controller is its cold inlet and unpack sends the value first \, so wired straight through every CC would go to the previous controller., f 56;
#X text 900 1080 + 1 because pgmout is 1-based (item 228): this inlet means the wire number \, 0 for the voice the FM-1's screen calls 001., f 60;
#X text 1300 870 The reject is a real error \, the opposite of u_map's: nothing comes back from the FM-1 \, so this is the only way to learn that u_map and this file disagree. C-8, f 66;
#X text 20 1300 WHAT IS NOT HERE: aftertouch \, pitch bend \, the mod wheel and sustain \, which the FM-1 takes and nothing here sends \; and any notion of what a note MEANS -- this file is told what to play and plays it. ⛔ CLOCK AND TRANSPORT ARE NOT HERE EITHER \, AND THEY DO NOT REACH THIS DEVICE AT ALL. They reach ONE port: u_tempo's realtime-out holds one midiout for them \, set at loadbang to port 1 -- the Launchpad. The FM-1 is port 4 and the nano is port 2 \, so neither has ever had a clock byte from this instrument. Measured with aseqdump on the hardware 2026-08-10 \, item 279: five seconds on Pd's Midi-Out 4 produced nothing at all. The FM-1 would follow a clock \, but only its own sequencer and arpeggiator do \, and Cut It plays it note by note., f 84;
#X text 900 1300 Velocity and program change work as the FM-1 ships: its MIDI channel on ALL (or 1) and its effect channel on 2 \, both on its GLO page (Reference \, m-vave-fm-1)., f 60;
#X text 1300 380 route leaves a remainder starting with a float \, which is a list \, so unpack takes it with no list append. program leaves the lone float that + 1 wants., f 76;
#X obj 20 1700 loadbang;
#X obj 20 1750 del 2000;
#X obj 20 1800 f \$1;
#X obj 20 1850 print m_fm1-channel;
#X text 300 1750 Prints the channel it got: nothing comes back from the FM-1 \, so a wrong channel is otherwise invisible. C-9, f 66;
#X obj 1400 1440 loadbang;
#X msg 1400 1500 expect m_fm1 none;
#X obj 1400 1560 s presence;
#X text 1750 1440 none is a kind: the FM-1 answers no device inquiry \, so it registers as undetectable on purpose rather than being left out by mistake. u_present's whole-rig re-wire still brings it back (ref/module/presence.md)., f 44;
#X obj 2300 660 unpack f f;
#X obj 2500 1900 r panic;
#X obj 2500 1960 t b b;
#X msg 2500 2020 0;
#X obj 2500 2080 ctlout 64;
#X text 2300 740 note bypasses makenote \, because a held key must not release itself: the off comes from the key \, as velocity 0 from u_map's fm1-key. The panic path covers the droning makenote prevents. It reuses the one noteout \, so MIDI_EXPECT stays noteout:2., f 62;
#X text 2700 1900 Panic is a note-off for every note \, 0 to 127 \, then sustain off (CC 64 at 0): the FM-1 ignores All Notes Off and All Sound Off (Reference \, m-vave-fm-1). The offs go to the one noteout as lists \, so they take the channel already in it., f 62;
#X obj 2400 660 t f;
#X obj 2400 900 midiout;
#X obj 2800 660 loadbang;
#X obj 2800 710 f \$1;
#X obj 2800 760 - 1;
#X obj 2800 810 div 16;
#X obj 2800 860 + 1;
#X text 2400 1000 byte: a raw byte \, out the FM-1's own port. A SysEx dump comes a byte at a time. Its channel must be 1., f 50;
#X obj 640 940 + 1;
#X obj 2760 2060 t b b;
#X msg 2760 2120 128;
#X obj 2760 2180 until;
#X obj 2760 2240 f;
#X obj 2760 2300 t f f;
#X obj 2900 2300 + 1;
#X msg 2760 2360 \$1 0;
#X msg 2900 2120 0;
#X text 1040 760 cc goes out one channel up: the FM-1 takes controllers for its effects alone \, on its effect channel \, 2 as it ships (Reference \, m-vave-fm-1)., f 30;
#X text 3020 2120 The right outlet first: the count starts again at 0 \, then until runs it 128 times \, each number a note-off. The t f f moves the count on before the number leaves. C-3, f 44;
